{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NUYD6ZMyBRKCqd2G4wwutp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum\n     2→title: \"Compute and verify SHA-1 digests via sha1sum\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go sha1sum binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary\n     6→  computes SHA-1 digests and prints them in GNU format, or verifies a checksum file.\n     7→  The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n     8→  reference binary (gsha1sum from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that\n     9→  their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n    10→\n    11→actor: Human Operator\n    12→\n    13→trigger: |\n    14→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd031-sha1sum.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    15→  a passing differential test for cmd/sha1sum.\n    16→\n    17→flow:\n    18→  - id: F1\n    19→    step: |\n    20→      The operator runs the Go sha1sum binary on a file or stdin.\n    21→      Example: sha1sum somefile.txt\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      cmd/sha1sum reads each file, computes its SHA-1 digest using crypto/sha1, and\n    25→      prints the result in GNU format to stdout.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      In check mode (--check), cmd/sha1sum reads a checksum file, recomputes each digest,\n    29→      and prints OK or FAILED for each entry.\n    30→  - id: F4\n    31→    step: |\n    32→      The differential testing harness executes both ./bin/sha1sum and gsha1sum with the\n    33→      same inputs and compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n    34→  - id: F5\n    35→    step: |\n    36→      The harness verifies exit codes. If outputs and exit codes match, the test passes.\n    37→  - id: F6\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      If they diverge, the harness reports the triggering args, both outputs, and both\n    40→      exit codes.\n    41→\n    42→touchpoints:\n    43→  - T1: \"cmd/sha1sum — SHA-1 digest computation, GNU format output, check mode, binary/tag flags (prd031-sha1sum R1, R2, R3)\"\n    44→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    45→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n    46→\n    47→success_criteria:\n    48→  - id: S1\n    49→    criterion: cmd/sha1sum compiles and ./bin/sha1sum exists after mage build.\n    50→  - id: S2\n    51→    criterion: The differential test for digest computation passes; output matches gsha1sum byte-for-byte.\n    52→  - id: S3\n    53→    criterion: The differential test for --check on a valid file passes; exits 0 and prints OK lines.\n    54→  - id: S4\n    55→    criterion: The differential test for --check on a file with a mismatch passes; exits 1 and prints FAILED.\n    56→  - id: S5\n    57→    criterion: The differential test for --tag passes; BSD format output matches gsha1sum --tag.\n    58→\n    59→out_of_scope:\n    60→  - SHA-1 is cryptographically broken; this implementation targets format compatibility only.\n    61→\n    62→test_suite: test-rel05.4\n    63→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51232ce4-c523-4362-91b9-8c0518fc2217","uuid":"7966c3d4-abb1-44b1-97d2-64d3f0864cdf","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/361/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum.yaml","content":"id: rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum\ntitle: \"Compute and verify SHA-1 digests via sha1sum\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go sha1sum binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary\n  computes SHA-1 digests and prints them in GNU format, or verifies a checksum file.\n  The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n  reference binary (gsha1sum from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that\n  their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd031-sha1sum.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/sha1sum.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go sha1sum binary on a file or stdin.\n      Example: sha1sum somefile.txt\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/sha1sum reads each file, computes its SHA-1 digest using crypto/sha1, and\n      prints the result in GNU format to stdout.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      In check mode (--check), cmd/sha1sum reads a checksum file, recomputes each digest,\n      and prints OK or FAILED for each entry.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness executes both ./bin/sha1sum and gsha1sum with the\n      same inputs and compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness verifies exit codes. If outputs and exit codes match, the test passes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If they diverge, the harness reports the triggering args, both outputs, and both\n      exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/sha1sum — SHA-1 digest computation, GNU format output, check mode, binary/tag flags (prd031-sha1sum R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/sha1sum compiles and ./bin/sha1sum exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: The differential test for digest computation passes; output matches gsha1sum byte-for-byte.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: The differential test for --check on a valid file passes; exits 0 and prints OK lines.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: The differential test for --check on a file with a mismatch passes; exits 1 and prints FAILED.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: The differential test for --tag passes; BSD format output matches gsha1sum --tag.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - SHA-1 is cryptographically broken; this implementation targets format compatibility only.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel05.4\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
